# Backend for production builds.
#
# These two values are public by design and are committed deliberately. The
# publishable key is not a credential: it grants exactly what row-level
# security allows, which for this project is "read everything, write nothing
# unless you are the allowlisted admin". It ships inside the JavaScript bundle
# of the deployed site either way, so a reader of this file learns nothing a
# visitor could not read from the page source. The RLS policies in
# supabase/001_panscreener.sql are the security boundary, not this key.
#
# To rotate: Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API keys, disable the
# old publishable key, then edit the value here.
#
# NEVER add the service_role or secret key to this file. That one bypasses
# row-level security entirely and would hand every visitor write access.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://rzhnmtfhlpviiagrnsdo.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_KUhNw2jUsYdxDd_P_RB5lg_aqYgW_MN
